                "text": "To solve  \n\\[\n\\sin(x)+x^2=42,\n\\]\nrewrite it as finding roots of\n\\[\nf(x)=\\sin(x)+x^2-42.\n\\]\n\nBecause \\(x^2\\) dominates, solutions should be near \\(x=\\pm\\sqrt{42}\\approx \\pm 6.4807\\). Using a numerical root-finder gives two real solutions:\n\n\\[\nx \\approx -6.497098216971565\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\approx 6.466650040905217\n\\]\n\nSo the equation has **two real solutions**, approximately \\(\\boxed{x\\approx -6.49710}\\) and \\(\\boxed{x\\approx 6.46665}\\).",
